    "updated_at": "2025-06-30T16:18:00Z",
    "body": "It seems reasonable to me to add an opt-in method name (or option in an options bag) to prevent focusing, with the understanding that the web developer will need to handle focus management themselves. I can imagine a variety of scenarios where a developer can come up with a more accessible solution that the current prescriptive methods (but I can also imagine many ways in which developers can make this _less_ accessible so we need to be a little careful here). \n\nI think it's worth fielding the opinions of accessibility practitioners here, though. Specifically I imagine @smhigley has some experience in this area, and would be able to offer some excellent insight.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
