    "created_at": "2026-06-06T21:23:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-06T21:23:20Z",
    "body": "coming in very late, but ... if a validation message is shown visually without also moving focus, in the first instance it will need to be announced to screen readers as a notification.\n\none confusing aspect of notifications happening on blur is usually that at that point, the user has already focused on the next form field, leading to a confusing experience - the user is now on field 2, but they hear the error for field 1 that they left already. i think a better example would be running validation while the user is still in the field, but they stopped typing/interacting",
